  "live_records": {
    "q-65054": {
      "dom_id": "step-q65054",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate ${f}_{zyx}(1,1,-1)$ for $f(x,y,z)=xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+z).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{z}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+z)) \\\\  & =xy\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{xy}{x+y+z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{zy}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{z}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zy}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{z}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{xy}{x+y+z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\cdot (x+y+z)-xy\\cdot (1)}{(x+y+z)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+xy+xz-xy}{(x+y+z)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+xz}{(x+y+z)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{zyx}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{zy}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zyx}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{zy}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}+xz}{(x+y+z)^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+z)\\cdot (x+y+z)^{2}-({x}^{2}+xz)\\cdot (2(x+y+z)\\cdot 1)}{(x+y+z)^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+z)(x+y+z)-2({x}^{2}+xz)}{(x+y+z)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate ${f}_{zyx}(x,y,z)$ at $(1,1,-1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zyx}(1,1,-1) & =\\frac{(2(1)+(-1))(1+1+(-1))-2({1}^{2}+1(-1))}{(1+1+(-1))^{3}}=\\frac{(1)(1)-2(0)}{(1)^{3}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
